// Rule: [T1574.002] Terminalfix - Lockscreencontentserver DUI70 Sideload
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1574.002
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceImageLoadEvents
// Purpose: Campaign-specific hunt for a legitimate Lock Screen binary loading a co-located malicious DirectUI DLL outside its standard Windows SystemApps location.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceImageLoadEvents for lockscreencontentserver dui70 sideload using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceImageLoadEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// TerminalFix - LockScreenContentServer.exe loads co-located dui70.dll outside SystemApps
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceImageLoadEvents
// Source behavior: Microsoft Security Research, published 2026-08-28
// A match identifies the source-observed sideload pair; it does not by itself prove TerminalFix compromise.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "LockScreenContentServer.exe"
| where FileName =~ "dui70.dll"
| extend LoadedDllDirectory = tostring(parse_path(FolderPath).DirectoryPath)
| where LoadedDllDirectory =~ InitiatingProcessFolderPath
| where not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith @"C:\\Windows\\SystemApps\\")
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessUniqueId,
          FileName, FolderPath, SHA1,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessAccountSid,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
